{
  "id": "ep474",
  "duration": 28.668,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.68,
      "text": "Saturn's giant rings completely vanish every fifteen years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Rings of Saturn -1 (4078770532).jpg",
        "credit": "Lunar and Planetary Institute from Houston, TX, USA",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rings_of_Saturn_-1_(4078770532).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.667,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.68,
      "end": 7.48,
      "text": "They span tens of thousands of miles, yet disappear from view.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn eclipse crop.jpg",
        "credit": "Saturn_eclipse.jpg: NASA/JPL/Space Science Institute\nderivative work: The High Fin Sperm Whale",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_eclipse_crop.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.667,
          "end": 7.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 7.48,
      "end": 11.22,
      "text": "Galileo Galilei first spotted mysterious bulges that looked like ears.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Galileo by leoni.jpg",
        "credit": "Ottavio Leoni",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galileo_by_leoni.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 7.467,
          "end": 11.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.22,
      "end": 14.58,
      "text": "When they disappeared, he admitted he was completely baffled.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Justus Sustermans - Portrait of Galileo Galilei, 1636.jpg",
        "credit": "Justus Sustermans",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Justus_Sustermans_-_Portrait_of_Galileo_Galilei,_1636.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.233,
          "end": 14.567,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 14.58,
      "end": 18.3,
      "text": "Astronomer Christiaan Huygens finally solved the mystery in 1659.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustrations de Systema Saturnium, sive de causis mirandorum Saturni phaenomenon... - (Non identifi\u00e9) ; Christian Huygens, aut. de texte - btv1b2600196j (07 of 10).jpg",
        "credit": "Huygens, Christiaan (1629-1695). Auteur du texte",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustrations_de_Systema_Saturnium,_sive_de_causis_mirandorum_Saturni_phaenomenon..._-_(Non_identifi%C3%A9)_;_Christian_Huygens,_aut._de_texte_-_btv1b2600196j_(07_of_10).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 14.567,
          "end": 18.3,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.3,
      "end": 21.46,
      "text": "He realized a flat, detached ring surrounded the planet.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Interior of Saturn.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Interior_of_Saturn.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 21.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.46,
      "end": 24.52,
      "text": "Spacecraft later measured the rings at just tens of meters thick.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA11668 The Tallest Peaks.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA11668_The_Tallest_Peaks.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.467,
          "end": 24.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.52,
      "end": 28.318,
      "text": "This exact alignment creates the illusion that the disk disappears.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Rings of Saturn -1 (4078770532).jpg",
        "credit": "Lunar and Planetary Institute from Houston, TX, USA",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rings_of_Saturn_-1_(4078770532).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.533,
          "end": 28.667,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
